{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat src/cljc/yang/correspondence.cljc && cat test/yang/correspondence_test.cljc'","aggregated_output":"(ns yang.correspondence\n  \"Structural checks for D1 records. These checks do not establish reliance:\n   all referenced content and relationships still require reconstruction.\"\n  (:require [dao.jing :as jing]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]))\n\n(def ^:private record-keys\n  #{:yang.correspondence/schema :yang.correspondence/evidence\n    :yang.correspondence/recipe :yang.correspondence/inputs\n    :yang.correspondence/roots :yang.correspondence/origin-bindings\n    :yang.correspondence/artifacts :yang.correspondence/metadata\n    :yang.correspondence/instruction-provenance})\n\n(def ^:private recipe-keys\n  #{:yang.correspondence.recipe/schema :yang.correspondence.recipe/function\n    :yang.correspondence.recipe/profile :yang.correspondence.recipe/input-roles\n    :yang.correspondence.recipe/evidence-contract :yang.correspondence.recipe/coverage})\n\n(defn- distinct-vector?\n  [v pred]\n  (and (vector? v) (every? pred v) (= (count v) (count (set v)))))\n\n(defn- role?\n  [entry]\n  (and (vector? entry) (= 2 (count entry)) (keyword? (first entry))\n       (int? (second entry)) (<= 0 (second entry))))\n\n(defn recipe?\n  \"Check the closed schema and basic shapes, without resolving the profile.\"\n  [x]\n  (and (map? x) (= recipe-keys (set (keys x)))\n       (= 1 (:yang.correspondence.recipe/schema x))\n       (qualified-symbol? (:yang.correspondence.recipe/function x))\n       (jing/segment-address? (:yang.correspondence.recipe/profile x))\n       (distinct-vector? (:yang.correspondence.recipe/input-roles x) role?)\n       (some? (:yang.correspondence.recipe/evidence-contract x))\n       (jing/segment-address? (:yang.correspondence.recipe/coverage x))))\n\n(defn- path-step?\n  [x]\n  (or (and (int? x) (<= 0 x))\n      (and (vector? x) (= 2 (count x))\n           (every? #(and (int? %) (<= 0 %)) x))))\n\n(defn- binding?\n  [entry]\n  (and (vector? entry) (= 2 (count entry))\n       (some? (first entry))\n       (let [k (second entry)]\n         (and (vector? k) (= 3 (count k))\n              (vm/occurrence-origin? (nth k 0))\n              (jing/segment-address? (nth k 1))\n              (vector? (nth k 2)) (every? path-step? (nth k 2))))))\n\n(defn- artifact?\n  [x]\n  (and (map? x) (= #{:format :identity :storage :derivation} (set (keys x)))\n       (keyword? (:format x)) (some? (:identity x))\n       (jing/segment-address? (:storage x))\n       (jing/segment-address? (:derivation x))))\n\n(defn correspondence?\n  \"Check the closed schema and basic shapes, not addresses or endpoints.\n   Compilation-scoped site uniqueness is checked during reconstruction.\"\n  [x]\n  (and (map? x) (= record-keys (set (keys x)))\n       (= 1 (:yang.correspondence/schema x))\n       (every? jing/segment-address?\n               [(:yang.correspondence/evidence x) (:yang.correspondence/recipe x)\n                (:yang.correspondence/metadata x)])\n       (distinct-vector? (:yang.correspondence/inputs x) jing/segment-address?)\n       (distinct-vector? (:yang.correspondence/roots x) jing/segment-address?)\n       (distinct-vector? (:yang.correspondence/artifacts x) artifact?)\n       (distinct-vector? (:yang.correspondence/instruction-provenance x) jing/segment-address?)\n       (distinct-vector? (:yang.correspondence/origin-bindings x) binding?)))\n(ns yang.correspondence-test\n  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n            [yang.correspondence :as correspondence]))\n\n(def address-a :segment/sha256-aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa)\n(def address-b :segment/sha256-bbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbb)\n\n(def recipe\n  {:yang.correspondence.recipe/schema 1\n   :yang.correspondence.recipe/function 'example/reconstruct\n   :yang.correspondence.recipe/profile address-a\n   :yang.correspondence.recipe/input-roles [[:source 0]]\n   :yang.correspondence.recipe/evidence-contract [:slice9-site-tables 1]\n   :yang.correspondence.recipe/coverage address-b})\n\n(def record-value\n  {:yang.correspondence/schema 1\n   :yang.correspondence/evidence address-a\n   :yang.correspondence/recipe address-b\n   :yang.correspondence/inputs [address-a]\n   :yang.correspondence/roots [address-b]\n   :yang.correspondence/origin-bindings [[0 [[:source :program [\"run\" 0] 0] address-b []]]]\n   :yang.correspondence/artifacts []\n   :yang.correspondence/metadata address-a\n   :yang.correspondence/instruction-provenance []})\n\n(deftest closed-structural-contracts\n  (is (correspondence/recipe? recipe))\n  (is (correspondence/correspondence? record-value))\n  (testing \"unknown keys and schema revisions are refused\"\n    (is (not (correspondence/recipe? (assoc recipe :extra true))))\n    (is (not (correspondence/correspondence? (assoc record-value :verified true))))\n    (is (not (correspondence/correspondence? (assoc record-value :yang.correspondence/schema 2)))))\n  (testing \"addresses, unique declarations, and persisted origin shapes are required\"\n    (is (not (correspondence/correspondence? (assoc record-value :yang.correspondence/evidence \"commit\"))))\n    (is (not (correspondence/correspondence? (assoc record-value :yang.correspondence/inputs [address-a address-a]))))\n    (is (not (correspondence/correspondence? (assoc record-value :yang.correspondence/origin-bindings [[0 [[:ephemeral :scope :run 0] address-b []]]]))))\n    (is (not (correspondence/correspondence? (assoc record-value :yang.correspondence/origin-bindings (vec (repeat 2 (first (:yang.correspondence/origin-bindings record-value))))))))))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794422563000-engineer-d1-durable-correspondence.prompt.md'","aggregated_output":"Created-GMT: 2026-11-11 18:42:43 GMT\nCreated-Local: 2026-11-12 01:42:43 +0700\nCoding-Agent: codex\nSession-ID: pending (provider-generated — capture thread.started.thread_id at dispatch)\n\n# Task: D1 — the durable correspondence record (:yang.correspondence/schema 1) + independent reconstruction verifier\n\nRole: VM Engineer (compiler provenance)\n\nImplementers:\n- Model: gpt-6.1-terra | Assigned: 2026-11-13 13:56 +0700 | Status: active | Rationale: the owner released the adoption queue (\"you got it\"); the implementation-routing directive (deepseek credits low → codex) makes codex the implementation lane; terra is the moderate-complexity tier and this brief is a bounded either/or envelope. PROBE-VERIFIED live 13:5x +0700. Reviewer for this round must be NON-GPT (glm-5.3 / qwen4-max-preview / hydrogen candidates).\n\n**DISPATCH GATE SATISFIED: cc3 landed (2c80a421), owner release received in-session 2026-11-13 (\"you got it\"), lane probe-verified. Dispatching.**\n\n## Where you work\n\nWorktree: `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-d1`, branch `d1-correspondence`, cut from `origin/master` @ `56cc5ca3` (post-cc3, post-port, post-kit, post-shell-refactor, post-primitive; includes the cljd gate `4d0d3e70` and the python adoption `8018005d`). Work ONLY there. ANTLR prerequisites pre-generated by the orchestrator (`build/antlr` populated; mise trusted; `bb` available via `export PATH=\"$HOME/.local/share/mise/shims:$PATH\"`). TDD: red first for every acceptance item. Commit NOTHING — the orchestrator commits after review.\n\n## POST-CC3 / POST-REFACTOR AMENDMENT (2026-11-13 — supersedes stale context below)\n\nSince this brief was drafted, three things landed on master; the inventory refresh (work item 0 of your dispatch) reconciles against THESE facts:\n\n1. **cc3 is LANDED** (`2c80a421`: `0ec036d1` feature + `897786cf` r7-r11): the provenance side artifact EXISTS — `publish-closure!` emits it outside the manifest hash; the oracle site→C1-key binding is LANDED IN TEST (`test-cc3-oracle-site-c1-binding`, `latte_oracle_test.clj`), including the rebind for the port's lowering (Phase 3r `8456c2e9`: stamp wrapper 3→2 applications, extraction `[:operands 1 :operands 1 :value]`, correspondence clause moved). D1's recipe pins the POST-port/post-rebind revision and cites the rebind note (`1794519755000-...reverification...findings.md` item 3 — the rebind mechanics D1's recipe must reproduce).\n2. **The shell refactor LANDED** (`c62266ad..6445f37a` + docs): `yin.shell.*` namespaces exist (`yin.shell.query/link-answer`, `yin.shell.dht/store/session/main`); `src/cljc/yin/repl/query.cljc` still exists on master but its link-answer moved. File references in the older sections below read against CURRENT master, not against the draft's assumptions.\n3. **The port + kit are LANDED** (`309fe842` + `ba3cc407`, plus `a3f7ab8d` cljd cell-heap fix): yang.clojure's exception lowering is the continuation encoding; `finally` expressible, one-catch pinned; the DHT-parity cljd incident fixed at `engine.cljc` heap-entry init.\n4. **Ownership update for the MUST-NOT list**: `semantic/linearize.cljc` + `derive.cljc` are now cc3's LANDED surface (not an in-flight cession) — the datom-lane bridge (item 5) MAY edit them if you choose bridge-over-restriction, one-writer discipline still applying (check the exception-track registry at dispatch).\n5. The kit contract test on master is GREEN post-port (9/159/0, 47/47 provenance rows at merged master) — the pre-port 87F/21E baseline references below are historical.\n\n## Goal and authority\n\nD1 is the durable correspondence record binding the LaTTe oracle's evidence to real C1 occurrences, plus its independent reconstruction verifier. Authorities, in order:\n- `collab/yang-clojure/1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md` §4 (the D1 envelope, verbatim-evidence rule, the recipe, independent reconstruction), §6.3 (bounds), §8 (acceptance sequence).\n- `collab/yang-clojure/1794344088000-orchestrator-cc3-d1-mob-reconciliation.md` — the mob's Q2 ruling (3/3): **separate companion file `test/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_correspondence.edn` referencing the `:version 1` `slice9_site_tables.edn` VERBATIM — never upgrade those bytes in place; K-keyed access is a verified query through the `:origin-bindings` relation, not a second attribution table; integer site ids are scoped per compilation; historical runs without retained admissions never acquire invented origins** (owner ruling U: origins are never minted).\n- `collab/yang-clojure/1794374077000-engineer-cc3-fix-r2.muse-wonder-1.0.findings.md` §P1-4 and cc3's landed code: the provenance side artifact cc3 publishes is D1's input; the **datom-lane entity→occurrence bridge is D1's stated dependency** (cc3 recorded the row-lane restriction — D1 either lands the bridge per design §2.4 or records the same restriction).\n- The landed cc3 chain: `git log` on `cc3-lowering-provenance` (merged to master at landing) — the provenance side artifact outside the manifest hash, the oracle site→K binding, the caller-path threading.\n\n## The work items (each = acceptance criterion)\n\n1. **The D1 envelope** — `:yang.correspondence/schema 1` per design §4.1: closed key set; `:evidence` names the v1 tables VERBATIM (address, never a copy); `:recipe`; `:inputs` (retrievable closures, not commit strings); `:roots`; `:origin-bindings` (evidence-local site id → persisted K, unique within the claimed compilation, endpoints validated); `:artifacts`; `:metadata` (the C1 rows' address); `:instruction-provenance`. Content-addressed via dao.jing; no self-address field.\n2. **The recipe record** — `:yang.correspondence.recipe/schema 1` per design §4.1: closed, versioned, naming the interpreter function, the exact reconstruction profile (frontend revision, grammar/options, expansion environment, recorded origins/attempts, transformations, canonicalization, site-table derivation, lowering rules), input roles, and the oracle's exact schema identity.\n3. **The companion file** — `test/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_correspondence.edn` carrying the D1 record for the pinned corpus, beside (never replacing) `slice9_site_tables.edn`. The v1 file's bytes, hash, and `:version` are untouched; a test pins that.\n4. **The independent reconstruction verifier** — per design §4.2's seven steps and the mob's Q1 conditions: verify addresses and schemas; verify each code image under its own execution contract; reconstruct the compilation under the exact recipe; re-derive the oracle site declarations from compiled AST argument expressions (not from the producer's serialized classifications); reconstruct every claimed binding with exact coverage and multiplicities; execute the attribution query over separately scoped relations; publish a separate verification result naming the verifier revision. **The verifier must not call the producer's derivation as its only check** (design §4.2's explicit warning about `latte_oracle_tables.clj`).\n5. **The datom-lane decision** — inherit cc3's restriction: either land the entity→occurrence bridge (design §2.4) or record the restriction as D1's own; no half-state.\n6. **Bounds** — declare the finite ceilings per §6.3 BEFORE the tagged verification run; the cc3 v2 bounded-run declaration (`1794390804000-cc3-bounded-run-declaration-v2.md`) is the precedent format; inherit its measured baselines and re-derive D1's own.\n\n## Bounded file ownership (initial; the dispatch-time inventory refresh is the first deliverable)\n\nMAY edit: `src/dev/latte_oracle_tables.clj`, `test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj`, the new companion file + its validator, `test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc`, `src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc` (only if a side-artifact handle is missing), and NEW files for the record/recipe/verifier under `src/cljc/yang/` (propose exact paths in findings).\nMUST NOT: `slice9_site_tables.edn` (bytes frozen), `vm/macro.cljc`, `semantic.cljc`/`ast_walker.cljc` (continuation seat), `yang/clojure.cljc` (port's until it lands — check the registry at dispatch), `semantic/linearize.cljc` + `semantic/derive.cljc` (cc3's, unless the datom bridge is in-scope per item 5 and the registry is clear), `core/prelude.cljc`, `dht.cljc`. STOP and record if a fix seems to need more.\n\n## Invariants\n\nOracleEvidence verbatim; origins never minted; failed reconstruction refuses reliance independently of code loadability; `:trusted` is never substituted for `:verifying`; the verifier's result is a separate published record — D1 cannot mark itself verified.\n\n## Verification (G0 laptop; suite-scale is shiva's at landing)\n\nThe round-trip test, the verifier against the pinned corpus, `yang.latte-oracle-test` affected deftests, kondo 0 errors on every touched file. The full oracle suite is shiva-scale — record, don't run.\n\n## Deliverable\n\nFindings per protocol; include the dispatch-time inventory refresh (design §8 step 2) as its own section: every changed contract, every read-only dependency, any stale citation found against then-current master.\n\nBegin the final response exactly with:\nCompleted-GMT: <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS GMT>\nCompleted-Local: <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS local-timezone-name>\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
