{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"head -55 src/cljc/dao/jing/mem.cljc; rg -n '\"'^'\"\\\\(defn (get|open|create|handle)' src/cljc/dao/jing/mem.cljc src/cljc/dao/jing.cljc | tail -20; sed -n '1,90p' test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj; rg -n 'kernel.*fixtures|fixture-corpus|kernel-cases' test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj | tail -30\"","aggregated_output":"(ns dao.jing.mem\n  \"An ephemeral, thread-safe, content-addressed in-memory DaoJing byte\n   store (docs/design/dao.jing.md, Materialization rule and Reads;\n   docs/design/dao.jing.cbor.md, Memory and files).\n\n   (create-content-mem) returns a plain-data byte-store handle carrying\n   :put-bytes-fn, :get-bytes-fn, :close-fn and the test-facing :entries-fn,\n   accepted by dao.jing/materialize!, dao.jing/get, and dao.jing/close!.\n   The handle embeds no intake stream and identifies no source: an address\n   is derived solely from a payload, and the store never records which\n   stream carried a value, so equal payloads converge on exactly one entry.\n\n   What the store holds is the canonical CBOR payload bytes of each value,\n   an immutable snapshot under its content address. The state lives only in\n   the closures: no atom or array is reachable through the handle, bytes\n   are copied on insertion and on retrieval, so no caller can change a\n   snapshot in place. No framing -- nothing here is ever re-ingested across\n   process death.\n\n   :put-bytes-fn is an atomic insert-if-absent. The caller-supplied address\n   must be a :segment/<algo>-... content address whose digest is the hash\n   of the bytes; otherwise it throws. An address already holding the same\n   bytes reports :present and is never overwritten; an address already\n   holding different bytes is an integrity-failure collision and throws\n   loudly. The CAS loop is linearizable under JVM contention. Operations\n   after close throw; close itself is idempotent.\"\n  (:require [dao.jing :as jing]\n            [dao.jing.cbor :as cbor]))\n\n\n(defn- validate-address-bytes!\n  \"Reject a put before any write: the address must be a valid segment\n   content address whose digest is the hash of exactly these bytes.\"\n  [address bs]\n  (when-not (jing/segment-address? address)\n    (throw (ex-info \"dao.jing.mem: not a segment content address\"\n                    {:address address})))\n  (when-not (jing/segment-bytes-match? address bs)\n    (throw (ex-info \"dao.jing.mem: content address does not match the bytes\"\n                    {:address address}))))\n\n\n(defn- put-bytes-fn\n  \"Backend effect for one byte store: atomic insert-if-absent of a copy of\n   the bytes. The winner of the CAS returns :inserted; an existing equal\n   snapshot returns :present; an existing unequal snapshot is a collision\n   and throws. The closed check happens inside the loop so the operation is\n   linearizable against close.\"\n  [state]\n  (fn [address bs]\n    ;; copy first: the caller owns bs and may change it at any moment, so\n    ;; validation and every later comparison see only the snapshot\n    (let [snapshot (cbor/copy-bytes bs)]\n      (validate-address-bytes! address snapshot)\n      (loop []\nsrc/cljc/dao/jing/mem.cljc:108:(defn create-content-mem\nsrc/cljc/dao/jing.cljc:483:(defn get\n(ns yang.latte-oracle-test\n  \"Pinned upstream LaTTe differential harness, slices 1-9 of the Yang gap\n   program. A executes the original library on Clojure. B executes explicit\n   portability source on Clojure; C compiles it through Yang for the walker\n   and semantic VMs. Slice 9 fails closed on the full kernel corpus. The\n   legacy classifier records historical blockers;\n   the context module additionally checks free-symbol admission before C.\n   Adaptations, operation sequences and scope departures live beside the\n   manifest in yang/latte_oracle/.\"\n  (:require [clojure.java.io :as io]\n            [clojure.java.shell :as shell]\n            [clojure.edn :as edn]\n            [clojure.set :as set]\n            [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n            [clojure.string :as str]\n            [clojure.walk :as walk]\n            [dao.jing.cbor :as cbor]\n            [clojure.tools.reader :as r]\n            [clojure.tools.reader.reader-types :as rt]\n            [yang.clojure :as yang]\n            [yang.clojure-test :as compiler-test]\n            [yang.core.call :as call]\n            [yang.core.uast :as u]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\n            [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]\n            [yin.vm.data :as data]\n            [yin.vm.module :as module]\n            [yin.vm.encoder :as encoder]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.rows :as rows]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.rows-support :as rows-support]\n            [yin.vm.values :as values]\n            [yin.vm.semantic :as semantic]\n            [yin.vm.semantic.derive :as derive]\n            [yin.vm.semantic.linearize :as linearize]\n            [yin.vm.ucf :as ucf]))\n\n\n(def ^:private manifest\n  (edn/read-string (slurp (io/resource \"yang/latte_oracle/manifest.edn\"))))\n\n\n(defn- ns-declaration-aliases\n  \"Alias -> full ns symbol, taken from the file's own (ns ...) declaration —\n   never invented: ::alias/kw must read as :that.real.ns/kw.\"\n  [ns-form]\n  (let [alias-map (atom {})\n        consume-spec (fn [spec]\n                       (when (sequential? spec)\n                         (let [lib (first spec)]\n                           (loop [xs (rest spec)]\n                             (when (seq xs)\n                               (if (= :as (first xs))\n                                 (do (swap! alias-map assoc (second xs) lib)\n                                     (recur (drop 2 xs)))\n                                 (recur (next xs))))))))]\n    (loop [clauses (rest (rest ns-form))]\n      (when (seq clauses)\n        (let [clause (first clauses)]\n          (if (and (seq? clause) (= :require (first clause)))\n            (do (loop [reqs (next clause)]\n                  (let [spec (first reqs)]\n                    (when (and (not (nil? spec)) (not (keyword? spec)))\n                      (consume-spec spec)\n                      (recur (next reqs)))))\n                (recur (next clauses)))\n            (recur (next clauses))))))\n    @alias-map))\n\n\n(defn- read-forms\n  \"Read one latte-kernel source file with reader conditionals resolved for\n   :clj, ::alias/kw keywords resolved against the file's own ns declaration,\n   and ::kw resolved against the file's own namespace — so the C leg compiles\n   the same keyword identities the upstream A leg runs.\"\n  [ns-sym]\n  (let [f (io/resource (str (str/replace (name ns-sym) \".\" \"/\") \".cljc\"))\n        pr (rt/source-logging-push-back-reader (java.io.PushbackReader. (io/reader f)) 1 (str f))\n        ns-form (r/read {:read-cond :allow :features #{:clj} :eof ::eof} pr)\n        declared-name (second ns-form)\n        aliases (ns-declaration-aliases ns-form)]\n    (binding [r/*alias-map* aliases\n              *ns* (the-ns (create-ns declared-name))]\n      (loop [acc []]\n        (let [form (r/read {:read-cond :allow :features #{:clj} :eof ::eof} pr)]\n          (if (= form ::eof) acc (recur (conj acc form))))))))\n\n\n(def ^:private all-forms\n  (into {} (map (fn [ns-sym] [ns-sym (read-forms ns-sym)])\n                (distinct (map :ns manifest)))))\n3347:        exercise-entries (kernel-exercise-entries inventory (:fixtures kernel-gate-corpus) results)\n3480:    (is (= (count (:fixtures kernel-gate-corpus)) (count (set (map :id (:fixtures evidence)))))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
