{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1100,1155p' src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc; sed -n '136,230p' src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc; sed -n '1,110p' src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"   NaN map keys and set elements inside data payloads are out of scope\n   and fail closed when lookup misses.\n\n   Scope boundary: the set branch assumes ordinary set semantics, at most one\n   element per `=`-equivalence class; a set built with a comparator that\n   admits several `=`-equal, metadata-distinct elements is out of scope, the\n   same class of pathological-input residual `dao.jing.md` documents for its\n   own encoder (pathological symbols, scalar metadata). That deferred case is\n   silent and order-dependent, not reliably fail-closed: which `=`-equal\n   element the lookup picks depends on traversal order, so a metadata\n   mismatch may throw or may be silently accepted.\"\n  [a b]\n  (and (= (meta a) (meta b))\n       (or (nil? (meta a)) (same-content? (meta a) (meta b)))\n       (cond (map? a) (and (map? b)\n                           (= (count a) (count b))\n                           (every? (fn [[k v]]\n                                     (and (contains? b k)\n                                          (let [[k' v'] (find b k)]\n                                            (and (same-content? k k')\n                                                 (same-content? v v')))))\n                                   a))\n             (set? a) (and (set? b)\n                           (= (count a) (count b))\n                           (every? (fn [e]\n                                     (same-content? e (some #(when (= e %) %) b)))\n                                   a))\n             (sequential? a) (and (sequential? b)\n                                  (= (count a) (count b))\n                                  (every? true? (map same-content? a b)))\n             :else (cbor/content= a b))))\n\n\n(defn ast->semantic-bytecode\n  \"Project a map AST to flat content-addressed rows (§6.1 codec boundary\n   projection). Returns `{:root row-id, :rows {row-id [row-id tag & slots]}}`.\n\n   Only the §2.3 slots of each node enter its row: `:eid`, `:macro?`,\n   `:yang/*` keys, non-`:application` `:tail?` marks, and any other key are\n   dropped. `sym`/`syms` slots lose all metadata; `data`/`key` payloads lose\n   reader positions at every depth and keep all other metadata. Defaults are\n   saturated per §2.4. Children are projected first, so a parent's body\n   commits to its children's ids; structurally identical subtrees mint one\n   id and are stored as one row (§4.4).\n\n   Two nodes that mint one id must have one content: the row is checked\n   against the stored row with `same-content?` (metadata at every depth,\n   leaves by `dao.jing.cbor/content=`), and a mismatch throws\n   \\\"Semantic bytecode address collision\\\" rather than letting one row silently\n   replace the other. No known input reaches that throw: the encoder hashes\n   symbol and collection metadata, and makes every NaN one quiet NaN, so two\n   NaN scalars are one row value. The guard is a defence against the encoder\n   and this check disagreeing.\"\n  [ast]\n  (let [rows (atom {})]\n    (letfn\n   distinct admission identities, because their `id`s differ.\"\n  [id]\n  {:yin.link.publish/scope-id id\n   :yin.link.publish/ordinal (atom 0)})\n\n(defn- scope-admission-token\n  \"The admission token a scope object draws for one publication: the\n   scope's own `id` plus the ordinal the scope's counter assigns. The\n   counter lives in the caller-owned scope object, never here.\"\n  [{:yin.link.publish/keys [scope-id ordinal]}]\n  ;; pr-str keeps the value's full identity — a keyword's namespace, a\n  ;; string's quoting, a symbol's name — so distinct caller-chosen ids\n  ;; (:a/publisher, :b/publisher, \"publisher\") never mint the same token\n  (keyword \"yin.vm.linker.publish.scope\"\n           (str (pr-str scope-id) \"#\" (swap! ordinal inc))))\n\n(defn- spec-admission-token\n  \"The default admission token: derived deterministically from the\n   publication specification's own durable identity — the module name\n   and the content address of its compiled tree — never from hidden\n   mutable state. Two publications of the same specification therefore\n   answer the same admission identity (an idempotent re-publication is\n   the same recorded admission), and distinct specifications never\n   share one, in this or any other publisher process. A composition\n   that admits the same specification more than once as separate\n   admissions passes an `:yin.link.publish/scope` (or an explicit\n   `:yin.link.publish/admission`) so the admissions stay distinct.\"\n  [{:keys [name]} tree]\n  (keyword \"yin.vm.linker.publish.publication\"\n           (str name \"::\" (:root tree))))\n\n(defn- publication-origin\n  \"The occurrence origin of the publication admission `token` names:\n   the publisher's own medium, the explicit admission token, member 0.\n   `token` is the publication's admission identity — the\n   `:yin.link.publish/admission` option when the composition pins one,\n   the `:yin.link.publish/scope` option's next drawn token when the\n   composition scopes the publisher, otherwise the token derived from\n   the publication specification's own durable identity. The origin is\n   an admission event's identity, not a function of the tree's content\n   alone: it is persisted in the side record at publication time and\n   retrieved from that record; nothing ever reconstructs it from the\n   root.\"\n  [token]\n  [:source :yin.vm.linker.publish/publish token 0])\n\n\n(defn- claims-call-sites?\n  \"True when map AST `ast` carries the C1 key anywhere. A hit inside a\n   literal payload is data, not a claim: extraction then finds no\n   markers and the module publishes unannotated, as it should.\"\n  [ast]\n  (boolean (some #(= :yang/call-site %) (tree-seq coll? seq ast))))\n\n\n(defn- call-site-claim\n  \"The C1 claim `ast` makes over its canonical `tree`: nil when it\n   carries no markers; `{:origin o :rows [...]}` in canonical-byte\n   order (`jing/canonical-compare`) when the extracted markers exactly cover the tree's eligible\n   application occurrences; `{:missing [...] :extra [...]}` when they\n   do not; `{:unsupported-version v :path p}` when a marker's value is\n   not version 1 — a claim rejection, never a silent acceptance of a\n   table a retriever would read as version 1.\"\n  [ast tree admission]\n  (when (claims-call-sites? ast)\n    (let [origin (publication-origin admission)\n          extracted (filter #(= :yang/call-site (nth % 3))\n                            (:frontend-metadata\n                              (vm/ast-side-tables ast tree origin)))\n          eligible (into #{}\n                         (map (fn [[r p]] [origin r p]))\n                         (vm/application-occurrences tree))\n          marked (into #{}\n                       (map (fn [[o r p _ _]] [o r p]))\n                       extracted)]\n      (or (when-let [[v p] (some (fn [row]\n                                   (let [v (nth row 4)]\n                                     (when (not (and (integer? v) (= 1 v)))\n                                       [v (subvec row 0 3)])))\n                                 extracted)]\n            {:unsupported-version v, :path p})\n          (if (= eligible marked)\n            {:origin origin, :rows (vec (sort jing/canonical-compare extracted))}\n            {:missing (vec (sort jing/canonical-compare (remove marked eligible))),\n             :extra (vec (sort jing/canonical-compare (remove eligible marked)))})))))\n\n\n(defn link-local\n  \"Link `format`'s image through the manifest `address` over `handle`'s\n   own content, `:verifying` with discharge deferred, as a serving\n   composition does (yin.vm.linker.dht.md 4.1): a fresh local runtime per\n   call, so no request reaches any peer.  `opts` overrides the link\n   options; its `:bounds` are the runtime's composition bounds (section\n   4.2 step 2), every one left out taking `linker/default-bounds`.\"\n  ([handle address format] (link-local handle address format nil))\n(ns yin.vm.ucf.rows\n  \"Version-3 row codec. Pure row construction, graph decoding and\n   discovery-order cursor-cell numbering (design note §1), then full task\n   transport for the semantic kernel (continuation design §7):\n   lift-task walks a machine at any boundary into an abstract task and emits it;\n   lower-task decodes, checks and restores one into a fresh receiver.\n   An abstract row is {:kind keyword :slots vector}. Structural references\n   contain abstract rows; values use [:lit d], [:row abstract-row], [:cursor-cell id].\n   A task's :cursor-cells row holds alternating source identities and :cursor-cell-body\n   rows. Install children are separate tasks with separate cursor-cell scopes.\n\n   The census is ordered numerically by n (draft §3, \\\"sorted by n\\\"), so\n   :yin.k/cc-10 follows :yin.k/cc-9; its keys must spell cc-N with no leading\n   zero, else :slot-kind.\n\n   Default value markers are plain maps {:yin.k/row abstract-row} and\n   {:yin.k/cursor-cell keyword}. A guest map whose sole key is :yin.k/row or\n   :yin.k/cursor-cell collides with them and is not portable: on encode and decode\n   every literal of that shape is refused :yin.k/non-portable. Explicit\n   markers use the caller value encoder.\"\n  (:require [dao.host.bytes :as bytes]\n            [dao.jing :as jing]\n            [dao.jing.cbor :as cbor]\n            [dao.stream.apply :as apply2]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\n            [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\n            [yin.vm.module :as module]\n            [yin.vm.values :as values]\n            [yin.vm.semantic.analysis :as analysis]\n            [yin.vm.semantic.code :as code]\n            [yin.vm.semantic.frame :as frame]\n            [yin.vm.semantic.scan :as scan]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.custody :as custody]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.remote :as remote]))\n\n\n(def profile {:yin.code/contract \"v4\" :yin.k/version 1})\n\n\n(def pending-table\n  {:next [:C]\n   :put [[:ref :stream] :V :D]\n   :ffi [:C :D :D]\n   :ffi-request [:D :V [:ref :stream] [:ref :stream] :C :D]\n   :link-request [:D :S [:ref :stream] [:ref :stream] :C :D :D :D]\n   :link-response [:D :S [:ref :stream] [:ref :stream] :C :D]\n   :install [:S :D]})\n\n\n(def completion-table\n  {:next [:C]\n   :put [[:ref :stream] :V :optional-D]\n   :ffi [:C :D :D]\n   :ffi-request [:D :V [:ref :stream] [:ref :stream] :C :optional-D]\n   :link-request [:D :S :D :optional-D]\n   :link-response [:D :S :D]\n   :install [:S :D]})\n\n\n(def row-table\n  \"Slot descriptors, excluding id and kind. :repeat/:pairs are variadic;\n   :refs is an ordered vector of structural references. :pending is\n   discriminated by pending-table. Nothing in this table is executable.\"\n  {:vec [:repeat :V] :list [:repeat :V] :set [:repeat :V]\n   :map [:pairs :V :V] :bindings [:pairs :S :V] :store [:pairs :D :V]\n   :env [[:ref :bindings] :optional-D]\n   :closure [:A :N :syms [:ref :bindings] :optional-D]\n   :prim [:S] :stream [:D :D] :reified [[:ref :act]] :parked-ref [:D]\n   :act [:A :N [:ref :env] [:ref :window] [:ref :k] :N]\n   :tail [:A :N [:ref :k]]\n   :run [:A :N [:ref :env] [:ref :window] [:ref :k]]\n   :ready [[:ref :act :tail] [:ref :completion] :V :optional-D [:ref :cursor-cells] :optional-V]\n   :completion :completion\n   :window [:pairs :N :V] :k [:repeat [:ref :kframe]]\n   :kframe [:A :N [:ref :env] [:ref :window] :N]\n   :wait [[:ref :act :tail] [:ref :pending]] :pending :pending\n   :module-store [:D [:ref :store]]\n   :parked-table [:pairs :D [:ref :act :tail]]\n   :install [:S :D :D :D [:ref :task]]\n   :cursor-cells [:pairs :C [:ref :cursor-cell-body]] :cursor-cell-body [[:ref :stream] :D]\n   :task [:N :D :D :D :N [:ref :bindings] [:ref :store]\n          [:refs :module-store] [:ref :parked-table] [:ref :cursor-cells]\n          :D :D [:refs :install] [:refs :wait] :optional-D :optional-V :optional-D [:refs :run] [:refs :ready]]})\n\n\n(defn node\n  [kind slots]\n  {:kind kind :slots (if (= :window kind)\n                       (vec (mapcat identity (sort-by first (partition 2 slots))))\n                       (vec slots))})\n\n\n(defn- refuse!\n  [status kind path]\n  (throw (ex-info \"Row codec refused data\"\n                  {:yin.k/status status :yin.k/kind kind :yin.k/path path})))\n\n\n(defn- bad!\n  [kind path]\n  (refuse! :yin.k/undecodable kind path))\n\n\n(defn- marker-shaped?\n  [x]\n  (and (map? x) (= 1 (count x)) (or (contains? x :yin.k/row) (contains? x :yin.k/cursor-cell))))\n\n\n(defn- check-literal-markers!\n  [x]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
